From adce8cc0eca73432e9061d8aaebe0b063d9d8775 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ahcrazy20-tech <307454315+ahcrazy20-tech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 10:29:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v5.4: fix wrong moves when playing Black (FEN mirror bug) +
 WebKit 5GB storage fix
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ACCURACY (نقلات غلط):
- reader.js now always reports an ABSOLUTE board: viewport-relative
  coords (lichess transform) are un-flipped on the JS side; chess.com
  square-XY was already absolute. Removed the second 180° mirror in
  EngineViewModel.ingest that corrupted the FEN every time the board
  was flipped (playing Black) -> engine advice for the wrong position.
- Fixed lichess transform parsing (was dividing % by 12.5, so lichess
  boards were never read at all); now supports % and px translates.
- Move diff now computed after un-flipping, so lastMoveUCI is correct
  on flipped boards too.
- FenBuilder: clear stale en-passant + reset halfmove clock when ply
  frames are skipped; never emits a stale EP square.
- FenValidator: much stricter (side field, castling field, pawn ranks,
  pawn/piece counts, adjacent kings) so corrupt reads are rejected with
  a visible 'Board read unstable' warning instead of silent bad advice.

STORAGE (5GB):
- StorageManager now measures and reports Library/WebKit + Library/Caches
  (the WKWebView site data that was invisible and growing unbounded).
- Auto-purge of WebKit cache-class data at every launch (login survives).
- New 'Wipe browsing data' button in Settings for a full clear.
- URLCache switched to memory-only (no on-disk growth from engine APIs).

Tests: tests/ has a DOM-mock suite for reader.js (26 checks) and a
Python port suite for FenBuilder/FenValidator (19 checks) — all green.
Version bumped to 5.4.0 (build 54).

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
